        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "16-9 The parties recognize that a formative assistance program can contribute to the enhancement of teachers' skills and growth. Such a program is not used to determine whether a teacher is performing satisfactorily. The formative assistance program shall be totally voluntary. Such a program shall include, but not be limited to peer coaching, mentoring, instructional coaching and self-evaluation. If a mentor teacher, instructional coach or peer coach is utilized, no data provided by or solicited from a mentor teacher, instructional coach, or peer coach will be used in a teacher's evaluation. Further, the District and the Association will not use mentor teachers, instructional coaches or peer coaches to testify in evaluation grievances or legal cases concerning a teacher's job performance.",
            "block_bbox": [
                29,
