        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "16-11 A teacher's overall evaluation may be considered unsatisfactory if: A) performance is unsatisfactory in one or more of the performance standards related to classroom teaching; B) when a teacher repeatedly demonstrates significant deficiencies in performance areas not related to classroom teaching. A teacher whose performance is deemed to be unsatisfactory shall be given notice of deficiencies. Any areas of deficiency or unsatisfactory performance shall be mentioned in specific detail in the evaluation (although positive qualities should, of course, also be noted), and a remediation plan will be submitted in writing to the teacher involved. Said remediation plan will include the following:",
